2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .SH "NAME"
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  shutdown \- Halt, power off or reboot the machine
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .SH "SYNOPSIS"
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .HP \w'\fBshutdown\fR\ 'u
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  \fBshutdown\fR [OPTIONS...] [TIME] [WALL...]
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .SH "DESCRIPTION"
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .PP
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  \fBshutdown\fR
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  may be used to halt, power off, or reboot the machine\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .PP
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  The first argument may be a time string (which is usually
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  "now")\&. Optionally, this may be followed by a wall message to be sent to all logged\-in users before going down\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .PP
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  The time string may either be in the format
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  "hh:mm"
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  for hour/minutes specifying the time to execute the shutdown at, specified in 24h clock format\&. Alternatively it may be in the syntax
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  "+m"
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  referring to the specified number of minutes m from now\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  "now"
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  is an alias for
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  "+0", i\&.e\&. for triggering an immediate shutdown\&. If no time argument is specified,
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  "+1"
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  is implied\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .PP
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  Note that to specify a wall message you must specify a time argument, too\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .PP
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  If the time argument is used, 5 minutes before the system goes down the
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  /run/nologin
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  file is created to ensure that further logins shall not be allowed\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .SH "OPTIONS"
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .PP
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  The following options are understood:
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .PP
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  \fB\-\-help\fR
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RS 4
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  Print a short help text and exit\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RE
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .PP
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  \fB\-H\fR, \fB\-\-halt\fR
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RS 4
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  Halt the machine\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RE
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .PP
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  \fB\-P\fR, \fB\-\-poweroff\fR
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RS 4
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  Power the machine off (the default)\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RE
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .PP
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  \fB\-r\fR, \fB\-\-reboot\fR
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RS 4
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  Reboot the machine\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RE
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .PP
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  \fB\-h\fR
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RS 4
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  The same as
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  \fB\-\-poweroff\fR, but does not override the action to take if it is "halt"\&. E\&.g\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  \fBshutdown \-\-reboot \-h\fR
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  means "poweroff", but
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  \fBshutdown \-\-halt \-h\fR
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  means "halt"\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RE
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .PP
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  \fB\-k\fR
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RS 4
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  Do not halt, power off, or reboot, but just write the wall message\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RE
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .PP
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  \fB\-\-no\-wall\fR
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RS 4
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  Do not send wall message before halt, power off, or reboot\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RE
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .PP
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  \fB\-c\fR
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RS 4
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  Cancel a pending shutdown\&. This may be used to cancel the effect of an invocation of
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  \fBshutdown\fR
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  with a time argument that is not
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  "+0"
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  or
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  "now"\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RE
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .PP
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  \fB\-\-show\fR
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .RS 4
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  Show a pending shutdown action and time if there is any\&.
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z RECV  .sp
2026-09-24T00:12:35Z console run done (ready=True)
